\begin{abstract}
A Deza graph $G$ with parameters $(n,k,b,a)$ is a $k$-regular graph with $n$ vertices such that any two  distinct vertices have $b$ or 
$a$ common neighbours, where $b \geqslant a$. The children $G_A$ and $G_B$ of a Deza graph $G$ are defined on the vertex set of $G$ such that every two distinct vertices are adjacent in $G_A$ or $G_B$ if and only if they have $a$ or $b$ common neighbours, respectively. In this paper we present a general approach to dual Seidel switching and investigate Deza graphs whose children  are strongly regular graphs.
\end{abstract}

\begin{keyword} dual Seidel switching \sep Deza graph \sep strictly Deza graph \sep strongly regular graph  
\vspace{\baselineskip}
\MSC[2010] 05C50\sep 05E10\sep 15A18
