   117	certificate-producing construction. It is Track B. Mechanically, square the
   118	displayed N, recover the child M by its common-neighbor counts, and match every
   119	row of N to a closed-neighborhood row of M. At hard this is 387,072 elementary
   120	adjacency comparisons before row matching. The compact route uses the fact
   121	that a closed L_2(8) neighborhood is a 15-vertex row-column cross whose packed
   122	labels XOR to its centre. An affine relabelling preserves that identity because
   123	15 is odd. Seven selected rows recover an affine P, so three layers cost 294
   124	XORs exactly.
   125	
   126	Generation. In original L_2(8) coordinates, one coordinate factor is a
   127	fixed-point-free affine transvection and the other is a nonzero translation;
   128	both are involutions and both move every coordinate. Their product P therefore
   129	moves each lattice vertex to a different row and column, making P a Seidel
   130	involution. Each layer then receives an independently sampled invertible
   131	affine relabelling that mixes all six coordinate bits. N=P(M+I) is assembled
